.TH SEE 1 "" "local-models"
.SH NAME
see \- read an image into text with a local vision model (the image never leaves this Mac)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B see
<image|paste|latest> [\(dqquestion\(dq] [\-\-ocr|\-\-ui] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read an image into text with a local vision model (the image never leaves this Mac).
.PP
Input: an image path, paste, latest, or a subcommand (count, odd, diff, more, history, show).
.PP
Output: plain text; \-\-json one object; \-\-ui \-\-json adds the parsed element list under .data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-ocr
EXACT text via Apple Vision (no model, ~instant); composes with \-\-crop
.TP
.B \-\-ui
UI\-inventory read for screenshots/mocks (KIND/LAYOUT/HIERARCHY/ELEMENTS/ICONS/PATTERNS/PALETTE)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-measure
skip the exact\-first step: go straight to the model read
.TP
.B \-\-menubar
screencapture the main\-display top strip and \-\-ui it (needs Screen Recording perm)
.TP
.B \-\-crop WxH+X+Y
read only this pixel window of the image (crop\-then\-read lifts recall)
.TP
.B \-\-region NAME
named crop: top|bottom (third) · left|right (half) · center (middle quarter)
.TP
.B \-\-only E5[,E6]
diff only: re\-run just these extractors (E3/E4/E5/E6), return the delta, no model
.TP
.B \-\-grid N
diff only: grid resolution 4\-64 for E5/E6 (default 8 icons / 16 UIs)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-read
diff only: evidence pack and plain summary, no model read
.TP
.B \-\-color C
count only: objects of this colour (red green blue yellow orange purple gray black white, or #hex)
.TP
.B \-\-filled\-only
count only: drop hollow outlines, keep solid shapes
.TP
.B \-\-min\-area N
count/odd: ignore blobs smaller than N pixels (default scales with image size)
.TP
.B \-\-json
one JSON object on stdout, no ANSI; with \-\-ui adds parsed .data (schema\-constrained)
.TP
.B \-\-glow
render the read through glow (TTY\-only, no\-op without glow)
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-model M
vision model (default: Qwen3\-VL on MLX, falling back to $VISION_MODEL = minicpm\-v4.6 when a big ollama model is resident or MLX fails); \-m mlx:<hf\-repo> uses the mlx\-vlm backend
.TP
.B \-\-mlx
route to the mlx\-vlm backend outside ollama (Qwen3\-VL, higher UI\-structure accuracy) = $UI_VISION_MLX
.TP
.B \-\-all
with more, open \-1 or show \-1: include reads from other terminals, agents and hooks
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B see ~/Desktop/shot.png \(dqwhat is the build id?\(dq
Exact text is read first, then the model.
.TP
.B see paste \(dqwhat does the error say?\(dq
Straight from the clipboard.
.TP
.B see latest
Your newest screenshot.
.TP
.B see shot.png \-\-ocr
The exact text, no model, about a second.
.TP
.B see dashboard.png \-\-ui
A sectioned inventory of a website or app UI.
.TP
.B see count squares.png \-\-color red
Only the red objects.
.TP
.B see diff a.png b.png \-\-no\-read \-\-json
The measured evidence only, no model.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The work ran and failed, or a check failed.
.TP
.B 2
Bad usage: unknown flag, missing value, unknown verb.
.TP
.B 10
Server down or a backend call failed.
.TP
.B 11
Model or backend not available.
.TP
.B 12
Input missing or unreadable (file, image, history entry, optional dependency).
.TP
.B 13
Wall\-clock timeout.
.TP
.B 127
A required program is not installed.
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled by the caller.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B logs/*\-history.jsonl
One JSON line per call. History is per terminal by default; \-\-all or LM_ALL=1 reaches every caller.
.SH SEE ALSO
lm(1), q(1), warm(1), imagine, review
